`member_history` reads identity and every declaration in one repeatable-read transaction,
using SQLx macros and the existing left join/grouping logic without LIMIT. Order remains
registration descending/null-last, source ID descending, occurrence ID ascending. Counts
come from the complete vector; a funding-less declaration remains a declaration.
Summation adds every occurrence with both amount and normalized nonempty currency into
BigDecimal; total `None` means no known amount, whereas exact cancellation yields zero.
Group by source category ID, retaining unknown IDs and original labels. Currency policy
must match funder whitespace normalization exactly; reuse a private adapter helper/value
rather than introduce a second trim rule. Raw entry currency remains available for history.
Recent support filters the complete ordered declarations through the canonical enum before
taking 20; gifts/visits/employment stay in totals and history, not this donations section.

The existing HTTP member response becomes `{member, declarations, summary, recent_support,
recent_support_limit}`; each declaration carries source category ID/name, never a client
classification list. Serialize BigDecimal with existing normalized plain-string conversion.
Remove obsolete declaration_limit, update its consumers and tests in the same change.
TS `MemberDetails` mirrors the response through existing unknown-boundary parsers; its
`Declaration` interface is shared by full history and recent support. No client summation.

`App.svelte` adds member-history route; `EntityDetails.svelte` retains shared identity/funder
view and delegates to `MemberSummary.svelte` / `MemberHistory.svelte`. Native summary/history
anchors preserve q/strictness. History date inputs use UTC registration calendar dates,
inclusive start/end; undated declarations appear only with no active date bounds. Reset
page when bounds change. Invalid/reversed ranges show a clear inline error. Empty filtered
results differ from no stored declarations. No category filter, export, or analysis feature.

Summary shows separate currency totals and signed horizontal category bars with exact
text values. A small pure decimal-string-to-scaled-BigInt helper computes bounded visual
widths relative to max absolute category amount; convert only the final 0–1000 ratio to
Number. Show negative bars/signs, explicit unavailable amounts, and missing-currency count.

## Synthesis decision
Candidate recommendation: one complete domain read and one endpoint shared by two pages.

## Tradeoffs accepted
- Accept downloading complete history on the summary page for one consistent simple API.
- Accept transient recent-support clones for an explicit server-owned filtered subset.
- Accept no historical-party inference or currency conversion; labels describe stored history.

## Alternatives considered
- Separate summary/history endpoints: hides payload size but duplicates read/query paths and
  requires a second DTO/loader outcome. Worth revisiting only with measured payload pressure.
- SQL aggregates plus bounded category-filtered recent query: hides data volume but repeats
  category and normalization policy between SQL and domain unless passed derived enum IDs.
  Requires more repository contracts and grouping logic than this dataset currently needs.

## Implementation reconciliation
Design only; no implementation deviations accepted.

## Open questions and risks
Which exact source IDs belong to each canonical variant? Fixtures are synthetic and the
worktree has no .env. Require a live distinct ID/name query or authoritative source payload
before implementing; never infer source IDs from display labels. Should loans be labelled
explicitly in the donations/support explanatory text? Preserve their source category scope.

## Next implementation step
Confirm source category IDs, then replace the bounded repository read and category placeholder.

